00:14:30.845 --> 00:14:32.885
So let's go on to our next step.

00:14:33.085 --> 00:14:35.905
Our next step is that we're going
to add our reactions together,

00:14:36.085 --> 00:14:37.745
almost like a big math problem.

00:14:37.755 --> 00:14:40.125
So we're going to add up all
the reactants, all the products.

00:14:40.615 --> 00:14:42.855
But the big thing is that we're
going to cancel anything that's

00:14:42.875 --> 00:14:47.054
matching on the left and the right,
almost like kind of like spectator

00:14:47.054 --> 00:14:48.745
ions from net ionic equations.

00:14:49.314 --> 00:14:52.045
So the first thing is like, just to
kind of point that out, it's like, you

00:14:52.074 --> 00:14:55.694
can see that, Hey, we have matching
electrons on the left and right.

00:14:56.015 --> 00:14:57.385
So they have to cancel.

00:14:57.425 --> 00:14:58.895
That's a mandatory.

00:14:58.905 --> 00:15:00.655
It won't, won't be correct without that.

00:15:01.025 --> 00:15:03.585
So we can see that the 6
electrons do that on both sides.

00:15:03.945 --> 00:15:08.355
Now, after that, we're going to cancel
