It's very easy to miss something, right?

00:15:51.849 --> 00:15:54.979
So we have 6 waters, the 2 aluminums.

00:15:55.430 --> 00:16:02.850
Now NO two minus aqueous, and then we're
gonna add the two aluminum hydroxides,

00:16:07.980 --> 00:16:12.600
and we wanna make sure that we get the
subscript order correct and then plus the

00:16:12.600 --> 00:16:19.210
NH three and then plus the hydrogen ion.

